# {{full_name}}

An [Animus](https://github.com/launchapp-dev/animus-cli) trigger backend for **{{name}}**.

> **Status:** **Planned for Animus v0.4.x.** The `TriggerBackend` trait
> is not yet designed, so this scaffold is intentionally stub-only. Once
> the protocol crate (`animus-trigger-protocol`) lands, this directory
> will gain a full skeleton matching the layout used by `subject/` and
> `provider/`.

## What this will be

Trigger backends ingest external events (Slack messages, generic
webhooks, file-system watchers, cron-style schedules, GitHub events,
PagerDuty incidents, ...) and translate them into Animus subjects or
direct workflow dispatch.

Anticipated wire shape (subject to change):

- `trigger/register` — declare what events the backend listens for.
- `trigger/event` — server-streaming notifications carrying the event
  payload, source metadata, and a routing hint.
- `health/check` — same shape as the subject/provider variants.

## Next steps

Until v0.4.x:

- Use a [`subject` plugin](https://github.com/launchapp-dev/animus-plugin-template/tree/main/subject)
  with a poll loop if you need to bridge an external event source today.
- Subscribe to the [Animus core repo](https://github.com/launchapp-dev/animus-cli)
  for the v0.4.x roadmap.

